  "term": "paraplegia",
  "definition": "Paraplegia is a severe or complete loss of movement in both legs and the lower part of the trunk. It is most commonly linked to disorders of the spinal cord, though some brain, peripheral nerve, neuromuscular, or muscle diseases can also lead to weakness affecting both legs.",
